zjot's own cases, in the format of the vendored djot.js files (see test_runner.zig).

Every expected output in this file was produced by djot.js 0.3.2 on 2026-10-23:

    npx -y @djot/djot@0.3.2 input.dj

Expectations are never written by hand. A case goes in only when zjot and djot.js
agree on it; where zjot deliberately differs from djot.js, the difference is written
down here instead of pinned as a case.

Deliberate differences from djot.js 0.3.2:

1. Block attributes do not survive a blank line, and a block attribute left pending
   when a container (block quote, list item, fenced div, footnote) ends is dropped.
   djot.js 0.3.2 applies `{.c}`, blank, `para` to the paragraph and carries `> {.c}`
   out of the quote onto the next block, but its own test suite (attributes.test,
   "If there is a blank line between, the attributes won't be applied") says it must
   not; zjot follows the suite. Checked 2026-10-23.


Heading ids: generated ids follow document order wherever the heading sits.
````
# Foo

> # Foo
.
<section id="Foo">
<h1>Foo</h1>
<blockquote>
<h1 id="Foo-1">Foo</h1>
</blockquote>
</section>
````

Heading ids: an explicit id met later does not rename an id already generated.
````
# Foo bar

{#Foo-bar}
Paragraph
.
<section id="Foo-bar">
<h1>Foo bar</h1>
<p id="Foo-bar">Paragraph</p>
</section>
````

Footnote heading ids follow the endnotes' order, not the definitions'.
````
[^a]:
    > # P

[^b]:
    > # Q

text[^b] [^a]
.
<p>text<a id="fnref1" href="#fn1" role="doc-noteref"><sup>1</sup></a> <a id="fnref2" href="#fn2" role="doc-noteref"><sup>2</sup></a></p>
<section role="doc-endnotes">
<hr>
<ol>
<li id="fn1">
<blockquote>
<h1 id="Q">Q</h1>
</blockquote>
<p><a href="#fnref1" role="doc-backlink">↩︎</a></p>
</li>
<li id="fn2">
<blockquote>
<h1 id="P">P</h1>
</blockquote>
<p><a href="#fnref2" role="doc-backlink">↩︎</a></p>
</li>
</ol>
</section>
````

A footnote definition's paragraph continues across an unindented line (lazy continuation).
````
[^n]: note
para

x[^n]
.
<p>x<a id="fnref1" href="#fn1" role="doc-noteref"><sup>1</sup></a></p>
<section role="doc-endnotes">
<hr>
<ol>
<li id="fn1">
<p>note
para<a href="#fnref1" role="doc-backlink">↩︎</a></p>
</li>
</ol>
</section>
````

Lazy continuation after a blank line and an indented line.
````
